---
import Button from "../components/ui/button";
import TextLink from "../components/ui/text_link.astro";
import Layout from "../layouts/layout.astro";
import { SquareArrowOutUpRight } from "@lucide/astro";
import ImageMarquee from "../components/ImageMarquee";

const experiences = [
  { company: "Mercurie", role: "Product Designer" },
  { company: "Tabs", role: "Founder & Design Lead" },
  { company: "Tempo AI (YC S23)", role: "Founding Product Designer" },
  { company: "Stealth AI Startup", role: "Founding Product Designer" },
  { company: "Luupli", role: "Senior Product Designer" },
  { company: "Vegeel", role: "Product Design Lead" },
  { company: "Freelance", role: "Product Designer" },
];
---

<script>
  import { animate } from "motion";

  const pulse = document.getElementById("pulse");
  const available = document.getElementById("available")!;

  document.addEventListener("mousemove", (e) => {
    available.style.left = `${e.clientX + 15}px`;
    available.style.top = `${e.clientY + 10}px`;
    available.style.position = "fixed";
  });
  pulse?.addEventListener("mouseenter", () => {
    animate(available, { opacity: 1 }, { duration: 0.3 });
  });
  pulse?.addEventListener("mouseleave", () => {
    animate(available, { opacity: 0 }, { duration: 0.1 });
  });
</script>

<Layout title="About">
  <main>
    <div class="mb-6">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
        <h1>Oluwadamilola ‘Dami’ Ojetunji</h1>
        <div
          id="pulse"
          class="relative cursor-pointer z-20 flex items-center justify-center"
        >
          <div
            class="absolute w-4 bg-[#E0FAEC] aspect-square rounded-full -z-10"
          >
          </div>
          <div class="w-2.5 aspect-square bg-[#1FC16B] rounded-full"></div>
        </div>
        <div
          id="available"
          class="px-2.5 absolute opacity-0 p-1 rounded-b-xl shadow-xl shadow-[#00000010] rounded-tr-xl rounded-tl-xs bg-[#FDEBFF] dark:bg-[#272727] border-border border"
        >
          <span class="text-[#620F6C] dark:text-[#F9C6FF] text-sm"
            >Available for New Opportunities</span
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <p>
        Architect-turned-product designer, Founder, Community builder,
        Traveller, Tennis player & Plant mom.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div
      class="overflow-hidden h-[340px] sm:mt-6 mt-4 sm:h-[600px] rounded-2xl"
    >
      <img
        src="/dami-ojetunji.jpg"
        class="rounded-2xl object-cover h-[600px] object-[55%_10%] -translate-y-[50px] sm:translate-y-0 sm:h-[600px] sm:object-[55%_0%] w-full"
        alt=""
      />
    </div>
    <div class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-8">
      <p>
        I’m genuinely fascinated by how things, people and communities work, why
        and how they work the way they do. This curiosity has been my north star
        through making key decisions in my design processes, solving complex and
        ambiguous problems, considering uniques contexts and nuances that could
        influence design decisions. all of which has guided me to consistently
        find the right solutions for the right people while scaling the company,
        users and the market at large for the last 5 years.
      </p>
      <p>
        I've done this as a founding product designer at teams like <TextLink
          href="https://ng.linkedin.com/company/vegeel"
          text="Vegeel"
        /> and <TextLink href="https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/tempo-2" text="Tempo AI (YC SC23)" /> and as a senior product
        designer at <TextLink href="https://apps.apple.com/ng/app/luupli/id6463861554" text="Luupli" /> and a myriad of other global
        teams across industries like AI, HealthTech, Cybersecurity, B2B, B2C, E-commerce,
        Fintech and more.
      </p>
      <p>
        On the side, I'm building <TextLink href="https://www.jointabs.com" text="Tabs" /> aka. 'Mobbin for
        Africa'. Tabs is a thoughtfully curated library of African digital products.
        It helps product designers, engineers, and product teams see how real products
        in Africa are solving design and usability challenges. Instead of relying
        on references from outside contexts, Tabs showcases screenshots categorised
        by industries, user flows, and features from African products, think onboarding,
        payment flows, error states, mobile screens dashboards, and more.
      </p>
      <p>
        To me, design is more than just ‘how it looks’ or ‘how it works’ but,
        ‘who it works for’. Design considers long term impact on a business, the
        users and non-users, and society at large. It has the power to include
        and exclude and has it’s consequences. it’s important to me to do the
        best I can from my little corner of the world to make it easier,
        thoughtful, beneficial, inclusive, and truly human-centred.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8">
      <h1 class="mb-4 text-[15px]">Experience (2020 - Present)</h1>
      <div class="flex flex-col mt-4 gap-1">
        {
          experiences.map((experience) => (
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center py-2 group">
              <p class="group-hover:font-normal">{experience.company}</p>
              <p class="group-hover:font-normal">{experience.role}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-8">
      <h1 class="mb-4 text-[15px]">Beyond the day-to-day</h1>
      <p>
        I also dedicate time to mentoring designers at all stages of their
        careers on platforms like <TextLink href="https://adplist.org/mentors/dami-ojetunji" text="ADPList" /> and through
        NGOs like <TextLink href="https://www.designchics.com/" text="Design Chics" /> , where I help train the
        next generation of people in design including underrepresented groups. I
        provide guidance on launching successful careers, how to thrive and remain
        relevant in the industry, refining design processes, working on cross-functional
        teams, and more. I also contribute to open-source and speak at industry events.
        When I'm not doing all that, you'll find me rewatching the office for the
        millionth time, annotating a new read, at a local rave, an art exhibition,
        or on the tennis court.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-[86px] mb-40">
      <ImageMarquee
        images={[
          "/slider1.jpg",
          "/slider2.png",
          "/slider3.jpg",
          "/slider4.jpg",
          "/slider5.jpg",
        ]}
        client:load
      />
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
